  "findings": [
    "Caller-provided lifeId and controllerId are only regex-normalized; they are not repository-bound identity, controller, consent, or authority evidence.",
    "The legacy spot engine consumes its replay nonce and advances counters before self-match rejection, allowing a rejected request to poison the nonce and mutate sequence state.",
    "A second spot engine duplicates the current native market cell and hardcodes KAIOS as quote asset while current main intentionally keeps the 11520 native quote candidate unfrozen.",
    "The settlement adapter is production fail-closed, but its local fixture can create VERIFIED_SETTLED records, CT values, volumes, candles, and ownership labels without a durable authoritative registry.",
    "Decimal input is gated through JavaScript Number and aggregate values use Number, permitting precision loss or non-finite behavior for large or high-precision values.",
    "Caller-controlled settledAtMs determines candle time instead of receipt-bound authoritative time.",
    "bindMatchedTrade does not bind the source trade marketId and substitutes the adapter marketId, so engine and market origin are not cryptographically linked.",
    "For custom tick or lot sizes, quote precision failures can occur after maker fills have already mutated orders and trades, so matching is not atomic or rollback-safe.",
    "Replay, order, trade, and settlement state is process-memory only and is not durable, globally atomic, or exactly once.",
    "The candidate mounts into a stale legacy shell and has no current V4.1 real-browser, responsive, accessibility, or screenshot evidence.",
    "The mount owns empty module-private market and settlement instances and exposes no live order or data-feed hookup, leaving the rendered panel static rather than an operational quote surface.",
